      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given $\\log_x 4=\\log_{27} 3$,\nwe can rewrite it as $\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x}=\\frac{\\log 3}{\\log 27}.$\n\nSince $\\log 3=\\log\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\log 27=3$, we have $\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x}=\\frac{\\log\\frac{1}{3}}{3}.$\n\nBy subtracting both sides, we get $\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x}=1-\\frac{\\log 3}{3}$. This simplifies to $\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x} = -\\frac{2\\log 3}{3}$.\n\nSince $\\log_3 4=\\frac{\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log 3}}{ \\frac{\\log 3}{3}}=\\frac{2}{3}$, we have $\\frac{\\log 2}{\\log x}=-\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nSince $\\frac{\\log 2}{\\log x}=\\log_2 x=\\log_2 2^{-2/3}=\\frac{2}{3}$, we can conclude that $x=8$.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\boxed{x=\\boxed{8}}.",
